<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>State is a snapshot (closure):</strong> When the event handler =
runs, <code>counter</code> is captured with its current value (0). All thre=
e <code>setCounter</code> calls use the same captured value: <code>counter =
+ 1 =3D 0 + 1 =3D 1</code>. React batches these updates and only applies th=
e last one, so the counter shows 1.</li>
<li><strong>Alert timing:</strong> The <code>alert</code> executes synchron=
ously before React re-renders, so it shows the old value (0).</li>
<li><strong>Batching:</strong> React batches multiple <code>setState</code>=
 calls in event handlers. Since all three calls set state to the same value=
 (1), the result is just 1.</li>
</ol>
