<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key takeaways:</strong></p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Custom hooks</strong> let you extract and reuse stateful logic =
across components.</li>
<li>Custom hook names <strong>must start with <code>use</code></strong> so =
React can enforce the rules of hooks.</li>
<li>A custom hook can use any built-in hooks (<code>useState</code>, <code>=
useEffect</code>, <code>useCallback</code>, etc.).</li>
<li>Always add a <strong>cleanup function</strong> in <code>useEffect</code=
> to prevent state updates on unmounted components.</li>
<li>Custom hooks make code easier to <strong>test in isolation</strong> and=
 to <strong>maintain</strong>.</li>
